<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Scope</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>chapter<sp/>focuses<sp/>on<sp/>`sattyre::SMTProblem`,<sp/>`parse_smtlib_file`,<sp/>and<sp/>basic<sp/>`SMTSolver`<sp/>contracts.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Early<sp/>SMT<sp/>support<sp/>is<sp/>text-oriented<sp/>and<sp/>intentionally<sp/>conservative.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>target<sp/>is<sp/>robust<sp/>ingestion<sp/>and<sp/>explicit<sp/>errors,<sp/>not<sp/>full<sp/>theory<sp/>reasoning.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">```text</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;sattyre/SattyreSMT.hpp&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">sattyre::SMTProblem<sp/>smt<sp/>=<sp/>sattyre::parse_smtlib_file(&quot;examples/example.smt2&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>(smt.smtlib.empty())<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>throw<sp/>std::runtime_error(&quot;SMT<sp/>input<sp/>unexpectedly<sp/>empty&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
